    "name": "doc",
    "op": "hlc_overflow",
    "doc": "Counter is at MAX_COUNTER (0xFFFF) and the merge logic would compute c_new = MAX_COUNTER + 1. Conformant implementations MUST detect this overflow and bump l_new += 1, c_new = 0. Silent wrapping to 0 without bumping l_new is a bug. The vector lists three starting states; each maps to an expected (l_new, c_new)."
  },
  {
    "name": "no_observe_same_ms_max",
    "op": "hlc_overflow",
    "start": {
      "l_old": 1700000000000,
      "c_old": 65535
    },
    "physical_time_ms": 1700000000000,
    "observe": null,
    "expected": {
      "l_new": 1700000000001,
      "c_new": 0
    }
  },
  {
